config: {}
doc: "Experiment 1: nonsharded model loading (1 drive, all four loaders).\n\nFull\
  \ 42 GB Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf on ONE drive (c1).\nEach loader path\
  \ reads all 42 GB from that single NVMe:\n\n  - mmap                        (built-in\
  \ kernel path with mmap)\n  - stream                      (built-in kernel path,\
  \ no mmap)\n  - xnvme io_uring_file         (kernel path with O_DIRECT)\n  - upcie-cuda\
  \                  (userspace P2P NVMe->VRAM)\n\nMPS disabled: exp1 confirmed MPS\
  \ helps kernel loaders 4-14% but\notherwise obscures loader identity. Keeping it\
  \ off across both\nexperiments for apples-to-apples."
status:
  elapsed: 103.0316390991211
  failed: 0
  passed: 9
  skipped: 0
  started: 1783517597.1396515
steps:
- description: 'One-shot: kill any lingering llama-cli / llama-completion / llama-server
    on the target and dump current GPU memory.'
  id: 001_kill_stray_cuda
  name: kill_stray_cuda
  nr: 1
  status:
    elapsed: 2.465134382247925
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517597.1403298
  uses: kill_stray_cuda
- description: Turn CUDA MPS off and reset compute mode to DEFAULT so subsequent processes
    see the whole VRAM.
  id: 002_disable_mps
  name: disable_mps
  nr: 2
  status:
    elapsed: 2.2654974460601807
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517599.6054835
  uses: disable_mps
- description: "\nPrepare a spare NVMe as the DMA target for xNVMe's upcie-cuda backend.\n\
    \nTwo layout modes are supported. Both end with the drive detached\nfrom the kernel\
    \ NVMe driver and bound to uio_pci_generic, and both\nemit an extents JSON that\
    \ the loader consumes via\nLLAMA_XNVME_DMA_EXTENTS.\n\n  layout=raw (default,\
    \ backwards compatible):\n    Copy the .gguf onto the raw device starting at LBA\
    \ 0 via dd.\n    The drive holds a raw byte image of the file; file offset O\n\
    \    trivially maps to LBA (O / lba_nbytes). The extents JSON has\n    a single\
    \ entry, [{file_offset: 0, lba: 0, length: file_size}].\n\n  layout=xfs-fiemap:\n\
    \    Format XFS on the drive, mount, copy the .gguf onto the FS as\n    a normal\
    \ file, run xfs_bmap (FIEMAP equivalent) to capture the\n    file's on-disk extents,\
    \ umount, then detach + bind as above.\n    The extents JSON carries one entry\
    \ per XFS extent with the\n    per-drive LBA computed from the physical block\
    \ offset. This is\n    the realistic \"user put their model on a real FS\" shape.\n\
    \nIn both modes the workflow's earlier setup_dataset step must have\nstaged the\
    \ model onto a *different* drive (the source drive,\nmounted at /mnt/gguf/model.gguf)\
    \ so llama.cpp can open the file for\nGGUF metadata reads during the run; the\
    \ DMA target here is the only\ndrive touched during bulk weight reads.\n"
  id: 003_prepare_dma_c1
  name: prepare_dma_c1
  nr: 3
  status:
    elapsed: 22.23663330078125
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517601.8709986
  uses: setup_dma_target
  with:
    defer_detach: 'true'
    dma_namespace: 1
    dma_pci_addr: 0000:c1:00.0
    fs_dst_name: model.gguf
    fs_mount_point: /mnt/dma-0
    gguf_extents_path: /root/full-c1.extents.json
    layout: xfs-fiemap
    source_gguf: /mnt/gguf-src/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf
- description: "\nCold-start measurement for llama.cpp with a configurable loader\
    \ path.\n\nDrops the OS page cache before each iteration, runs llama-completion\n\
    with ``-n 1`` so it stops as soon as one token is produced, and\nrecords the wall-clock\
    \ and max RSS via /usr/bin/time. The interval\nis dominated by the weight-load\
    \ phase, so it is the \"seconds to\nfirst token\" figure of merit.\n\nThe same\
    \ script drives every loader variant so their cijoe outputs\nland side by side\
    \ under the same step template. Pass:\n\n    loader:    mmap | stream | xnvme\
    \ | default\n    direct_io: true | false\n    xnvme_be:  io_uring_file | libaio_file\
    \ | thrpool_file | ...\n\nUses llama-completion rather than llama-cli because\
    \ upstream\nrefactored llama-cli into a chat-only REPL; llama-completion is the\n\
    tty-free one-shot binary.\n"
  id: 004_run_mmap
  name: run_mmap
  nr: 4
  status:
    elapsed: 19.598007440567017
    failed: 0
    passed: 1
    skipped: 0
    started: 1783517624.107642
  uses: run_baseline
  with:
    gguf_path: /mnt/dma-0/model.gguf
    iterations: 1
    llama_bin: /root/llama.cpp/build/bin/llama-completion
    loader: mmap
    n_gpu_layers: 999
    n_tokens: 1
    prompt: hi
